From: Yash Hooda <yash.hooda6@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:58:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Fix GitHub namespace: yashhooda1, not hoodarunner
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The badge URLs and gh command assumed one namespace for everything.
They are two: GitHub is yashhooda1, while hoodarunner is the Ollama and
HuggingFace handle. `gh repo create hoodarunner/...` fails outright.

Only the GitHub references change. The Ollama model name stays
hoodarunner/selfevolve-reviewer — it has to match the Ollama username or
the push is rejected — and ollama/README.md now says so explicitly, so
the two don't get conflated again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YEPpTfqvKcxQrfaydM28UE
---
 README.md        | 6 +++---
 ollama/README.md | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

